                    About the Role



Do you love weddings? We're looking for a passionate, relationship-driven Manager, Wedding Sales & Marketing to lead our sales and marketing efforts while creating an exceptional experience for engaged couples. In this role, you'll oversee the customer journey from initial inquiry through booking, helping couples select the perfect photography and videography packages to capture one of the most important days of their lives.



You'll conduct consultations via phone and Zoom, manage the sales pipeline, optimize CRM processes, collaborate with cross-functional teams, and contribute to the growth of our sales organization by hiring and mentoring future tea
mbers. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who thrives in consultative sales, hospitality, and customer experience.



Key Responsibilities

}~} Conduct phone and Zoom consultations to understand each couple's wedding vision, preferences, timeline, and budget.

}~} Recommend personalized photography and videography packages that align with each couple's needs.

}~} Clearly explain package options, pricing, add-ons, timelines, and booking processes.

}~} Manage the entire sales pipeline from inquiry to signed contract.

}~} Perform timely follow-ups through phone,
, text messaging, and CRM automation.

}~} Maintain accurate customer records, notes, and sales activities within the CRM.

}~} Develop expertise in CRM automations, workflows, templates, messaging, and reporting.

}~} Monitor sales performance and consistently work toward monthly booking and revenue goals.

}~} Stay informed about wedding trends, photography styles, videography innovations, and customer preferences.

}~} Partner with marketing and production teams to ensure a seamless transition from booking to project execution.

}~} Help improve sales processes, customer experience, and operational efficiency.

}~} Recruit, onboard, train, and mentor additional Wedding Consultants and Sales Representatives as the team grows.

}~} Support marketing initiatives that generate qualified leads and strengthen brand awareness.

}~} Deliver exceptional customer service throughout every stage of the client journey.



Required Qualifications

}~} 3+ years of experience in consultative sales, customer success, hospitality, event planning, or a related field.

}~} Proven ability to meet or exceed sales targets and performance goals.

}~} Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills with a warm, professional, and engaging personality.

}~} Strong consultative selling and relationship-building abilities.

}~} Excellent verbal and written English communication skills.

}~} Comfortable conducting video consultations and presentations via Zoom.

}~} Highly organized with strong time management and multitasking skills.

}~} Experience managing CRM systems and customer pipelines.

}~} Ability to work independently in a remote environment.

}~} Availability to work evening hours (1:00 PM – 10:00 PM CST).



Preferred Qualifications

}~} Passion for weddings, photography, and event planning.

}~} Experience in the wedding, hospitality, luxury service, or events industry.

}~} Leadership or team management experience.

}~} Experience hiring, coaching, or mentoring sales professionals.

}~} Knowledge of marketing automation and customer engagement strategies.

}~} Experience with high-ticket consultative sales.

}~} Familiarity with customer journey optimization and sales process improvement.



